# The rest of Arrigal's camp by the lake (lane 28, 2026-10-08: "more people walking around and doing things"): Stoica
# mending his nets on the shore, Old Paraschiva at the pot, Gavril with the horses, Mihnea walking the camp's edge, and
# a camp dog. Unvoiced for now.

~ fisher
Stoica: Nets tear. You mend them. The lake's the same. It takes a little and you mend what's left.
Stoica: Don't wade in past your knees. The bottom drops away, and nothing that goes down there comes back up the same.
-> END

~ cook
Old Paraschiva: Sit if you want to eat, stand if you want to be looked at. Luvash's wine is for Luvash, and for me when he isn't looking.
* Heard anything interesting? -> svalich_road/the_counts_huntsman:cook_news
* Goodbye. -> END

~ groom
Gavril: This one bites, that one kicks, and the black one is Arrigal's, so don't touch it at all. The others are good horses. They know the way out of the valley. They just can't take it.
-> END

~ lookout
Mihnea: Keep to the fire, stranger. I watch the road so you don't have to. And so I see who comes down it.
-> END

~ dog
Narrator: The camp dog trots after you for a few steps, decides you aren't carrying anything to eat, and goes back to sitting very hopefully beside the pot.
* [if spell:speak_with_animals] Ask the dog about the camp. -> dog_speaks
* [if not spell:speak_with_animals] [knows:speak_with_animals] (Cast Speak with Animals, and ask the dog about the camp.) -> dog_cast
* [if spell:speak_with_animals or knows:speak_with_animals] Leave it by the pot. -> END
-> END

~ dog_cast
cast speak_with_animals
if check.last
-> dog_speaks
endif
-> END

# Speak with Animals (2024 PHB): the camp dog saw Bluto carry Arabelle off to the lake (Curse of Strahd, Vallaki).
~ dog_speaks
Narrator: The dog keeps one eye on the pot while it talks, the way a sentry keeps one eye on the road.
if flag.arabelle_rescued or flag.arabelle_lost
Narrator: "The little one's back, or she isn't. The big man in the red sash stopped shouting. The pot's still the pot."
-> END
endif
if quest.missing_arabelle == asked
quest missing_arabelle clue
Narrator: "The little one went out in the dark in a sack, on the shoulder of the man who smells of the lake and no fish. North, to the water. I barked. The man in the black coat told me hush."
-> END
endif
if quest.missing_arabelle == clue
Narrator: "The lake-and-no-fish man. North, by the water. Go. Why are you still here?"
-> END
endif
if not quest.missing_arabelle
quest missing_arabelle rumored
endif
Narrator: "The big man in the red sash shouts at the lake and drinks. His little one is gone from her bed. Nobody looks for her, because the man in the black coat said don't. I sit with the big man. I'm a good dog."
-> END
